1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
The Remote

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:10,040
Hey, Simka! The button got stuck on the remote!

3
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,040
How can we get it back out of there?

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,400
Look and learn, Nolik!

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,400
Please help!

6
00:00:15,919 --> 00:00:18,039
Come on, come on, come on, come on, come on!

7
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:22,920
Oh, oh, oh! Should I let it go now?

8
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:23,920
Oops!

9
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,000
Nolik, hide somewhere!

10
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:51,500
Nolik, she stole the remote!

11
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,900
Nolik, where are you hiding?

12
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:57,800
Hello there, Fixies!

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,399
Hey, where are you?

14
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,359
Hey, Tom Thomas! You got here just in time!

15
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:04,719
Chewsocka ran off with the TV remote!

16
00:01:04,959 --> 00:01:07,359
And so what? I can turn it on without it!

17
00:01:07,599 --> 00:01:09,799
And my favorite cartoon is just about to start!

18
00:01:09,799 --> 00:01:13,319
Forget about the cartoons, will you? Nolik is missing!

19
00:01:13,519 --> 00:01:15,920
I'm afraid Nolik hid inside of the remote!

20
00:01:16,039 --> 00:01:17,640
And Chewsocka took it!

21
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:20,280
Oh no, Nolik's in big time trouble!

22
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:23,519
Tom Thomas, there must be something you can do!

23
00:01:23,719 --> 00:01:25,840
Chewsocka! Chewsocka!

24
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:27,400
Come here!

25
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:35,120
Where is that dog hiding? I'm going to go look in the other rooms.

26
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:41,780
Simka! Tom Thomas! Here I am! I'm over here!

27
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:45,900
For now, I'll wait here.

28
00:01:46,799 --> 00:01:49,939
Shusaka's not out there. Where are you? Hey, Simka!

29
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:52,939
I ran to get a pack-o-mat!

30
00:01:53,579 --> 00:01:55,079
What are you going to do with it?

31
00:01:55,079 --> 00:01:58,319
I'm going to search for the infrared ray that comes out of the remote.

32
00:01:58,439 --> 00:01:59,759
That's so great!

33
00:02:00,079 --> 00:02:01,039
But what is it?

34
00:02:01,359 --> 00:02:02,879
I'll explain it to you.

35
00:02:04,959 --> 00:02:08,560
Inside of most remote controls there's a special type of light bulb

36
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:11,719
called a light emitting diode, or LED for short.

37
00:02:12,039 --> 00:02:16,800
When we press a button, the LED sends an invisible infrared ray.

38
00:02:17,319 --> 00:02:20,960
And in the TV there is a receiver for these invisible rays.

39
00:02:21,199 --> 00:02:24,879
The TV understands the command that comes from the remote control

40
00:02:24,879 --> 00:02:28,560
and carries it out, like changing the channel or the volume.

41
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:39,159
If the rays are invisible, then how is it possible to see them?

42
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:43,000
In the pack-o-mat I've got these special goggles that can help me.

43
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,280
And now what?

44
00:02:46,479 --> 00:02:47,560
Yell to Nolik!

45
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:50,639
Get him to close the contact on any one of the buttons.

46
00:02:50,919 --> 00:02:51,960
Nolik!

47
00:02:52,039 --> 00:02:54,519
You've got to push one of the buttons down on the remote!

48
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:57,400
A button? But how am I going to do that?

49
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,120
Wait, one second!

50
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:01,439
Chewsock-a-Chewsocks with her brain full of rush!

51
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:04,240
Meow!

52
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,680
Meow!

53
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:09,960
Oh, mamma mia! Now she'll eat me together with the remote!

54
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:15,360
Nothing for you here.

55
00:03:15,439 --> 00:03:16,960
But here's something!

56
00:03:20,719 --> 00:03:21,719
There he is!

57
00:03:22,879 --> 00:03:24,200
He's over there!

58
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:30,600
Chew-saca, come here. Do you want a hot dog?

59
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:34,680
So you want to play tough. All right, then.

60
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:51,780
Hooray! You're in one piece! How did you find me?

61
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,140
By looking out for the remote's rays.

62
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:57,520
It's just a shame it's impossible for me to see them.

63
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:59,719
What are you saying? You can!

64
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:06,000
If you want to see infrared rays, all you have to do is look through a digital camera.

65
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,320
Try it for yourself!

66
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,920
Turn on the camera on a mobile telephone.

67
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:13,320
Now go ahead and press any button on the remote control

68
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:15,760
and point the camera towards the front of it.

69
00:04:15,879 --> 00:04:18,560
You'll see a bright dot on the screen of the camera.

70
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,639
That's the light-emitting diode working!

71
00:04:20,639 --> 00:04:24,560
It's letting off a special light that can't be seen by the naked eye.

72
00:04:25,759 --> 00:04:28,959
It's also possible to point the remote control at a mirror,

73
00:04:29,079 --> 00:04:34,079
and then through the camera you can see how the light-emitting diode turns itself on.

74
00:04:34,279 --> 00:04:38,079
So what that means is that invisible rays bounce off of a mirror

75
00:04:38,079 --> 00:04:40,439
in the same way that regular light does.

76
00:04:41,159 --> 00:04:46,039
So you can control the TV by bouncing the light from a remote control off of a mirror.

77
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,439
You don't believe me?

78
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,639
Then go ahead and try it yourself!

79
00:04:50,639 --> 00:04:58,240
By the way, if your toys weren't all stuffed under the bed we would have found the remote without the goggles.

80
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:02,039
Don't worry about it. When the cartoons are over, I'll put them away.

81
00:05:05,839 --> 00:05:08,560
So, you done watching? Time to clean up!

